# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the CPU, memory, and GPU resources for a managed workflow, and define sizes that match the size of the problem."
msgstr "Elige los recursos de CPU, memoria y GPU para un workflow gestionado y define tamaños que se ajusten al tamaño del problema."

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a compute profile"
msgstr "Elegir un perfil de cómputo"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a compute profile {#choose-a-compute-profile}"
msgstr "Elegir un perfil de cómputo {#choose-a-compute-profile}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Managed workflows run on compute profiles. A compute profile is a fixed combination of vCPUs, memory, and GPUs, similar to the resources that you request from an HPC scheduler. When you upload a workflow, you map its sizes, such as `S` and `M`, to profiles, and each run picks one of those sizes. The job then runs on its own node with that profile, and keeps the profile until the job ends.\n"
msgstr "Los workflows gestionados se ejecutan en perfiles de cómputo. Un perfil de cómputo es una combinación fija de vCPU, memoria y GPU, similar a los recursos que solicitas a un planificador de HPC. Cuando subes un workflow, asocias sus tamaños, como `S` y `M`, a perfiles, y cada ejecución elige uno de esos tamaños. Después, el trabajo se ejecuta en su propio nodo con ese perfil y lo conserva hasta que el trabajo termina.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Profile | vCPUs | Memory (GB) | GPUs |\n"
"| - | - | - | - |\n"
"| `8x32` | 8 | 32 | None |\n"
"| `16x128` | 16 | 128 | None |\n"
"| `48x768` | 48 | 768 | None |\n"
"| `128x1500` | 128 | 1500 | None |\n"
"| `24x120x1l40s` | 24 | 120 | 1 L40S |\n"
"| `20x320x2a100` | 20 | 320 | 2 A100 |\n"
"| `80x1200x8a100` | 80 | 1200 | 8 A100 |\n"
"| `160x1792x8h100` | 160 | 1792 | 8 H100 |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Perfil | vCPU | Memoria (GB) | GPU |\n"
"| - | - | - | - |\n"
"| `8x32` | 8 | 32 | Ninguna |\n"
"| `16x128` | 16 | 128 | Ninguna |\n"
"| `48x768` | 48 | 768 | Ninguna |\n"
"| `128x1500` | 128 | 1500 | Ninguna |\n"
"| `24x120x1l40s` | 24 | 120 | 1 L40S |\n"
"| `20x320x2a100` | 20 | 320 | 2 A100 |\n"
"| `80x1200x8a100` | 80 | 1200 | 8 A100 |\n"
"| `160x1792x8h100` | 160 | 1792 | 8 H100 |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A profile ID has the form `{cpu}x{memory}`, with memory in GB, or `{cpu}x{memory}x{count}{gpu}` for a profile with GPUs. For example, `24x120x1l40s` has 24 vCPUs, 120 GB of memory, and one NVIDIA L40S GPU.\n"
msgstr "Un ID de perfil tiene la forma `{cpu}x{memory}`, con la memoria en GB, o `{cpu}x{memory}x{count}{gpu}` para un perfil con GPU. Por ejemplo, `24x120x1l40s` tiene 24 vCPU, 120 GB de memoria y una GPU NVIDIA L40S.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check available profiles {#check-available-profiles}"
msgstr "Comprobar los perfiles disponibles {#check-available-profiles}"

