# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Look up a profile by its resources {#look-up-a-profile-by-its-resources}"
msgstr "Buscar un perfil por sus recursos {#look-up-a-profile-by-its-resources}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead of typing a profile ID, you can describe the resources that your workflow needs with `compute_profile()`, and use the result as a value in `sizes_map`. Pass `cpu` and `memory` in GB, and pass `gpu` for a GPU profile:\n"
msgstr "En lugar de escribir un ID de perfil, puedes describir los recursos que necesita tu workflow con `compute_profile()` y usar el resultado como valor en `sizes_map`. Pasa `cpu` y `memory` en GB, y pasa `gpu` para un perfil con GPU:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A `sizes_map` accepts profile IDs and the profiles that `compute_profile()` returns, and you can mix both in one map. To check a profile ID before you upload, pass it to `compute_profile()`, for example `client.compute_profile(\"16x128\")`. If no profile matches, the error lists the available profiles.\n"
msgstr "Un `sizes_map` acepta ID de perfil y los perfiles que devuelve `compute_profile()`, y puedes mezclar ambos en un mismo mapa. Para comprobar un ID de perfil antes de subir, pásalo a `compute_profile()`, por ejemplo `client.compute_profile(\"16x128\")`. Si ningún perfil coincide, el error lista los perfiles disponibles.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`compute_profiles()` returns a list, so you can also filter it yourself. For example, the following code finds the GPU profiles:\n"
msgstr "`compute_profiles()` devuelve una lista, así que también puedes filtrarla tú mismo. Por ejemplo, el siguiente código encuentra los perfiles con GPU:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set a default compute profile for your workflow {#set-a-default-compute-profile-for-your-workflow}"
msgstr "Establecer un perfil de cómputo predeterminado para tu workflow {#set-a-default-compute-profile-for-your-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Most workflows start with one size. Map it to a profile with `sizes_map`, and make it the default with `default_size`, when you upload the workflow:\n"
msgstr "La mayoría de los workflows empiezan con un solo tamaño. Asócialo a un perfil con `sizes_map` y conviértelo en el predeterminado con `default_size` cuando subas el workflow:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every run of the workflow uses this profile, so you do not need to pass a size when you run it:\n"
msgstr "Todas las ejecuciones del workflow usan este perfil, así que no necesitas pasar un tamaño cuando lo ejecutas:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: match sizes to problem sizes {#best-practice-match-sizes-to-problem-sizes}"
msgstr "Buena práctica: ajusta los tamaños a los tamaños de los problemas {#best-practice-match-sizes-to-problem-sizes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A workflow solves specific problems, and it might require different compute profiles as the problems increase in scale and complexity. With a `sizes_map` for each workflow, you can do the following:\n"
msgstr "Un workflow resuelve problemas específicos y puede requerir distintos perfiles de cómputo a medida que los problemas crecen en escala y complejidad. Con un `sizes_map` para cada workflow, puedes hacer lo siguiente:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Give large problems enough compute resources to run to completion.\n"
msgstr "Dar a los problemas grandes recursos de cómputo suficientes para que se ejecuten hasta el final.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prevent small problems from using a larger node than they need.\n"
msgstr "Evitar que los problemas pequeños usen un nodo mayor del que necesitan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can base the sizes on the factors that determine your workflow's memory and CPU use, such as the subspace size, the number of batches, or the number of qubits.\n"
msgstr "Puedes basar los tamaños en los factores que determinan el uso de memoria y CPU de tu workflow, como el tamaño del subespacio, el número de batches o el número de qubits.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the sizes {#define-the-sizes}"
msgstr "Definir los tamaños {#define-the-sizes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can map up to four sizes, for small (`S`), medium (`M`), large (`L`), and extra-large (`XL`) problems. For example, the following code defines a workflow with three sizes:\n"
msgstr "Puedes asociar hasta cuatro tamaños, para problemas pequeños (`S`), medianos (`M`), grandes (`L`) y extragrandes (`XL`). Por ejemplo, el siguiente código define un workflow con tres tamaños:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Size rules {#size-rules}"
msgstr "Reglas de tamaño {#size-rules}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Size labels must be `S`, `M`, `L`, or `XL`, so a workflow can define up to four sizes. A managed workflow matches labels in uppercase or lowercase, and stores them in uppercase. Two sizes can map to the same profile.\n"
msgstr "Las etiquetas de tamaño deben ser `S`, `M`, `L` o `XL`, así que un workflow puede definir hasta cuatro tamaños. Un workflow gestionado reconoce las etiquetas en mayúsculas o minúsculas y las almacena en mayúsculas. Dos tamaños pueden asociarse al mismo perfil.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A workflow rejects the first upload in the following cases:\n"
msgstr "Un workflow rechaza la primera subida en los siguientes casos:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A label is not `S`, `M`, `L`, or `XL`.\n"
msgstr "Una etiqueta no es `S`, `M`, `L` ni `XL`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "You set `sizes_map` without `default_size`, or `default_size` without `sizes_map`.\n"
msgstr "Estableces `sizes_map` sin `default_size`, o `default_size` sin `sizes_map`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`default_size` is not one of the labels in `sizes_map`.\n"
msgstr "`default_size` no es una de las etiquetas de `sizes_map`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A value in `sizes_map` is not an available compute profile.\n"
msgstr "Un valor de `sizes_map` no es un perfil de cómputo disponible.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Change sizes on re-upload {#change-sizes-on-re-upload}"
msgstr "Cambiar los tamaños al volver a subir {#change-sizes-on-re-upload}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you upload the workflow again with the same `title`, the managed workflow handles the sizes as follows:\n"
msgstr "Cuando vuelves a subir el workflow con el mismo `title`, el workflow gestionado trata los tamaños de la siguiente manera:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you set `sizes_map`, the new sizes replace all of the stored sizes.\n"
msgstr "Si estableces `sizes_map`, los nuevos tamaños reemplazan todos los tamaños almacenados.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you omit `sizes_map`, the workflow keeps the stored sizes and the default.\n"
msgstr "Si omites `sizes_map`, el workflow conserva los tamaños almacenados y el predeterminado.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To change only the default, set `default_size` without `sizes_map`. The value of `default_size` must be one of the stored sizes.\n"
msgstr "Para cambiar solo el predeterminado, establece `default_size` sin `sizes_map`. El valor de `default_size` debe ser uno de los tamaños almacenados.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set `default_size` every time that you set `sizes_map`. A re-upload does not require `default_size`. If the new sizes do not include the old default, the workflow has no default, and every run without `function_size` fails.\n"
msgstr "Establece `default_size` cada vez que establezcas `sizes_map`. Una nueva subida no exige `default_size`. Si los nuevos tamaños no incluyen el predeterminado anterior, el workflow no tiene predeterminado y toda ejecución sin `function_size` falla.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a size for each run {#choose-a-size-for-each-run}"
msgstr "Elegir un tamaño para cada ejecución {#choose-a-size-for-each-run}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass `function_size` to `run()` to choose one of the workflow's sizes for that job. If you omit it, the job uses the workflow's default size:\n"
msgstr "Pasa `function_size` a `run()` para elegir uno de los tamaños del workflow para ese trabajo. Si lo omites, el trabajo usa el tamaño predeterminado del workflow:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`sizes()` and `get_default_size()` return the sizes that were stored when you loaded the workflow. To see sizes that changed after you loaded the workflow, load it again.\n"
msgstr "`sizes()` y `get_default_size()` devuelven los tamaños que se almacenaron cuando cargaste el workflow. Para ver los tamaños que cambiaron después de cargar el workflow, cárgalo de nuevo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To read the size and compute profile of the job, call `get_function_size()` and `get_compute_profile()` in your workflow code:\n"
msgstr "Para leer el tamaño y el perfil de cómputo del trabajo, llama a `get_function_size()` y `get_compute_profile()` en el código de tu workflow:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot sizes {#troubleshoot-sizes}"
msgstr "Solucionar problemas de tamaños {#troubleshoot-sizes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| The upload fails with `Invalid size '...'. Valid sizes are: S, M, L, XL.` | A label in `sizes_map` is not one of the four supported labels. |\n"
"| The upload fails with `Unknown compute profile '...' for size '...'.` | A value in `sizes_map` is not an available profile. Check the ID with `compute_profiles()`, or use `compute_profile()` to look it up. |\n"
"| `compute_profile()` fails with `No compute profile matches ...` | No profile has exactly those resources. For a GPU profile, also pass `gpu`. Pick a profile from the list in the error. |\n"
"| The upload fails with `'default_size' is required when 'sizes' is provided.` | The first upload sets `sizes_map` without `default_size`. |\n"
"| `run()` fails with `Unknown function size '...' for this function. Available sizes: ...` | The workflow does not define the size that you passed to `function_size`. |\n"
"| `run()` fails with `This function has no size.` | A re-upload replaced the sizes and removed the default. Upload again with `default_size`, or pass `function_size`. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problema | Causa |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| La subida falla con `Invalid size '...'. Valid sizes are: S, M, L, XL.` | Una etiqueta de `sizes_map` no es una de las cuatro etiquetas admitidas. |\n"
"| La subida falla con `Unknown compute profile '...' for size '...'.` | Un valor de `sizes_map` no es un perfil disponible. Comprueba el ID con `compute_profiles()` o usa `compute_profile()` para buscarlo. |\n"
"| `compute_profile()` falla con `No compute profile matches ...` | Ningún perfil tiene exactamente esos recursos. Para un perfil con GPU, pasa también `gpu`. Elige un perfil de la lista del error. |\n"
"| La subida falla con `'default_size' is required when 'sizes' is provided.` | La primera subida establece `sizes_map` sin `default_size`. |\n"
"| `run()` falla con `Unknown function size '...' for this function. Available sizes: ...` | El workflow no define el tamaño que pasaste a `function_size`. |\n"
"| `run()` falla con `This function has no size.` | Una nueva subida reemplazó los tamaños y eliminó el predeterminado. Sube de nuevo con `default_size` o pasa `function_size`. |\n"
